				1003,
				8
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Terminal RPC handlers into file-per-struct modules\n\nExtract all gRPC entry points within `Source/RPC/CocoonService/Terminal` into dedicated PascalCase modules to align with the project-wide architectural convention. New modules cover the full terminal lifecycle: `OpenTerminal` (spawning PTY via `TerminalProvider::CreateTerminal`), `CloseTerminal` (disposing via `DisposeTerminal`), `TerminalInput` (forwarding bytes to the master writer), `ResizeTerminal` (emitting dimensions to Sky), and notifications for `AcceptTerminalOpened`, `AcceptTerminalClosed`, `AcceptTerminalProcessData`, and `AcceptTerminalProcessId`.\n\nEach handler implements the `Fn` signature required for Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro and bridges the `Vine` gRPC protocol to the `Sky` UI layer. Notifications are emitted via Tauri events (`sky://terminal/create`, `/exit`, `/data`, `/processId`, `/resize`) using lossy UTF-8 decoding for stream data. This completes the decomposition of the `CocoonService` namespace, ensuring consistent symbol resolution and maintainability across the terminal subsystem.",
			"SHA": "1a89bda0e090338927fd29676be62533ef50ca16"
		}
	],
